From 1efc4fe039af5e3cb7e5a77143165cc8853c8e59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Captain Polliwog build <build@captainpolliwog.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 18:26:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 53/57] WebCore: cheaper repaints, selection gaps and custom
 properties

Three costs the Speedometer profiles showed on a G4:
- Every repaint called -[NSView setNeedsDisplayInRect:], which walks the view
  tree inside an Objective-C exception guard. They are now collected and
  handed to AppKit once per run loop pass, or as one rectangle when that
  covers little more (10% on Speedometer's TodoMVC-JavaScript-ES5).
- A selection change walked every layer of the page twice, to repaint and to
  clear block selection gaps, even when no layer had any. RenderView now
  remembers whether any layer recorded gaps.
- RenderStyle::checkVariablesInCustomProperties walked the whole inherited
  custom property map, hundreds of entries on pages built with a design
  system, although only the properties this element set can be unresolved.
  StyleCustomPropertyData now tracks those.
